ead":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":394.15386586044866,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.05163493284431099,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":33.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.02440903039629412,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":25.2,"_gate_pool_share":0.32323215536018557,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.0036491016428394363,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":53.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.014339269963947321,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":27.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.01688088813613209,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":71.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0043576066754562985,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.047059998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":31.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Custom Truck One Source, Inc. provides specialty equipment rental and sale services to electric utility transmission and distribution, telecommunications, rail, forestry, waste management, and other infrastructure-related industries in the United States and Canada. It operates through two segments: Specialty Equipment Rentals (SER); and Specialty Truck Equipment and Manufacturing (STEM). The company owns new and used specialty equipment, including truck-mounted aerial lifts, cranes, service trucks, dump trucks, trailers, digger derricks, and other machinery and equipment. It offers new equipment for sale to be used for end-markets, which can be modified to meet customers specific needs. In addition, the company provides truck and equipment maintenance and repair services; and rents and sells specialized tools, including stringing blocks, insulated hot stick, and rigging equipment, as well as sale of specialized aftermarket parts. The company was formerly known as Nesco Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Custom Truck One Source, Inc. in April 2021. The company was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in Kansas City, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ryan  McMonagle | CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $778K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 262%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Custom Truck One Source, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.3B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 53% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5283232628398791},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Custom Truck One Source (CTOS) Could Be 24% Undervalued As Earnings Turn Positive","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-ctos/custom-truck-one-source/news/custom-truck-one-source-ctos-could-be-24-undervalued-as-earn","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794267637.542,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.912,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (CTOS) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/Understanding_the_Setup:_CTOS_and_Scalable_Risk_110726121001_1794028201.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794028201.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CTOS